Numerical reference facts in src/reference-vectors.json:
  David A. Vallado, Paul Crawford, Richard Hujsak and T. S. Kelso,
  "Revisiting Spacetrack Report #3," AIAA 2006-6753.
  https://celestrak.org/publications/AIAA/2006-6753/
  Selected TLEs and numerical outputs from SGP4-VER.TLE / tcppver.out, also
  available in the python-sgp4 reference-data mirror at revision
  8126f773923c2902719d45aab8bdb5cce86cf39d:
  https://github.com/brandon-rhodes/python-sgp4/tree/8126f773923c2902719d45aab8bdb5cce86cf39d/sgp4
  Cases 00005, 04632 and 08195; positions km, velocities km/s, time minutes
  since epoch, TEME frame. These are selected published numerical facts,
  not copied Python/C++ implementation code. No python-sgp4 runtime added.

Independent implementations / public standards, no source copied:
  STAC 1.0.0 item structure: https://github.com/radiantearth/stac-spec/tree/v1.0.0
  The metadata is STAC-style, not a complete STAC API/conformance claim.
  All custom hash/size/provenance fields use the infinitum: namespace.
  Free-space loss: Friis equation with c = 299792458 m/s.
  Thermal noise: kTB with k = 1.380649e-23 J/K.
  Scheduling: independently written bounded priority-first greedy intervals.

